@heading
Checklist of needs
@description
Personalized checklist for establishing family usage of the
property as applied to landscape design.
@content
     Every family should make a checklist of needs and
expectations before landscaping a property; these inventories
will list prospective usage of the public, private, and service
areas of the yard.  The ~public areas~ are usually in the front
of the house.  Landscape design elements here consist of the
driveway, walkway and ~foundation planting~.  Special
consideration should be given to off street parking areas and
privacy from the road.  The ~outdoor living area~ is where the
family will spend most of its time and each member will have an
impact on decisions for its development.  Things to think about
are the family's lifestyles; is there a need for space to
entertain, for children to play, for a patio or deck, for
specialized gardening, for a swimming pool?  The ~service area~
will be the place where the vegetable garden, tool shed, or
compost pile would go.All of the considerations should be put
into a checklist to be applied to the landscape design.  